{
  "version": "1",
  "description": "Hydra effect harvest (McGrath et al. 2023, arXiv:2307.15771): resample-ablate one attention layer at the final token (ablation axis: layers 8/13/18/23/28; resample-source axis: six seeded derangement columns, averaged per prompt by the test - the paper averages ~15 resample patches) and harvest every attention layer's output plus the final residual and total-effect logits, clean and ablated - the clean forward interns across all 30 points. Direct effects are computed post-hoc by the test with the paper's frozen-norm linearized unembedding DE_r(l) = (gamma * a_l / rms(h_final_r))^T W_U[ml_token] - an in-document subtraction edit measured R^2 0.09 and a whole-residual injection 0.30, both contaminated by RMSNorm renormalization, which the paper freezes. The test regresses, per ablation layer, the summed downstream compensatory effect on the ablated layer's own clean DE and asserts best-layer R^2 >= 0.6 (VeriFires floor; paper: 0.92 on Chinchilla 7B). Data: 128 factual-recall prompts, ml_token = clean argmax (gen_hydra.py).",
